.TH HTML2PDF-PHP 7 "2026-10-26" "html2pdf-php" "PHP extensions"
.SH NAME
html2pdf-php \- HTML to PDF in PHP: the html2pdf extension and its SC\eHtml2Pdf class
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
$pdf = new SC\eHtml2Pdf(string $html, array $options = []);
$pdf\->save(string $filename): void
$pdf\->output(): string
$pdf\->pageCount(): int
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The html2pdf extension turns HTML and CSS into a PDF, from inside PHP.
The content is cut into pages between lines of text, images and boxes, never
through them, under a header and over a footer with page numbers; a table of
contents, bookmarks, working links, embedded fonts and passwords come with it.
.PP
There's no browser behind it: the HTML and CSS are laid out by litehtml, by
Yuri Kobets and its contributors, and the PDF is written by simply-cpp's own
PDF engine, as a standards-compliant PDF (ISO 32000-1, PDF 1.7).
.PP
The document is laid out when the object is made, so \fBpageCount\fR() is known
straight away; \fBsave\fR() writes it to a file and \fBoutput\fR() gives it as a
string, to send to a browser or store.
.SH METHODS
.TP
\fB__construct\fR(string \fI$html\fR, array \fI$options\fR = [])
Lays out \fI$html\fR with the options below.
.TP
\fBsave\fR(string \fI$filename\fR): void
Writes the PDF to \fI$filename\fR, replacing a file of that name.
.TP
\fBoutput\fR(): string
The PDF's bytes.
.TP
\fBpageCount\fR(): int
How many pages it has.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are given by name in \fI$options\fR.
A name it doesn't know throws, so a typo shows straight away.
Lengths are in millimetres.
.TP
\fBsize\fR (string)
The paper: A3, A4, A5, letter or legal, in any case.
Default: A4.
.TP
\fBlandscape\fR (bool)
Turn the pages sideways.
Default: false.
.TP
\fBmargins\fR (array)
Any of \fBtop\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBbottom\fR, \fBleft\fR and \fBfirst_top\fR, the
first page's top margin (room for a letterhead; null for the same as
\fBtop\fR).
Default: top 10, right 10, bottom 10, left 30, first_top 60.
.TP
\fBheader\fR, \fBfooter\fR (string)
HTML above and below the content of every page (see HEADERS AND FOOTERS).
.TP
\fBcss\fR (string)
A stylesheet for the content, header and footer.
.TP
\fBbase_url\fR (string)
What relative links, images and stylesheets are found against: a folder,
file or URL.
.TP
\fBmedia\fR (string)
The type \fB@media\fR rules match: print or screen.
Default: print.
.TP
\fBtoc_page\fR (int)
Put a table of contents on this page, pushing what was there after it; 0 for
none.
Default: 0.
.TP
\fBtoc_title\fR (string)
The table of contents' title.
Default: Table of Contents.
.TP
\fBoutline\fR (bool)
The bookmarks a PDF reader shows: the table of contents' entries, or else the
h1 to h3 headings.
Default: true.
.TP
\fBmetadata\fR (array)
The document's information by name: Title, Author, Subject, Keywords, Creator
or your own.
The title defaults to the HTML's <title>.
.TP
\fBuser_password\fR, \fBowner_password\fR (string)
Encrypt the PDF: the user password opens it, and readers who use it may only
print; the owner password allows everything.
.TP
\fBbuiltin_fonts\fR (bool)
Set the text in PDF's own Helvetica, Times and Courier, which every reader
has: nothing embedded, smaller files.
Default: false.
.TP
\fBsplit_boxes\fR (bool)
Let a box's background, border or image be cut across two pages, as browsers
print them, instead of moving one that fits on a page to the next one whole.
Default: false.
.TP
\fBdraw_margins\fR (bool)
Outline the margins, header and footer, to check a layout.
Default: false.
.TP
\fBimage_resolution\fR (float)
PNG images are written at most about this many pixels per inch, at the
biggest size they're shown; 0 keeps them as they are.
Default: 150.
.SH "HEADERS AND FOOTERS"
In a header or footer, \fB#Page#\fR and \fB#ToPage#\fR become the page's number
and the last page's, and \fB#section#\fR, \fB#subsection#\fR and \fB#subtitle#\fR
the text of the last such element on or before the page.
In a header, an element with id="P1Head" shows on the first page only, and
one with id="POHead" on the others.
.PP
In the content, every <section> starts a new page and a line in the table of
contents, and so does an element styled page\-break\-before: always;
page\-break\-inside: avoid keeps an element on one page when it fits on one.
.SH ERRORS
Every failure throws an \fBSC\eException\fR (an \fBException\fR): an unknown
option or paper size, margins or metadata that aren't an array, a negative
toc_page, a file that can't be
written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a PDF to the browser:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$pdf = new SC\eHtml2Pdf(\(aq<h1>Invoice</h1><p>Due in 30 days.</p>\(aq);
header(\(aqContent\-Type: application/pdf\(aq);
echo $pdf\->output();
.fi
.RE
.PP
A report with a header, page numbers and a table of contents, saved:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$pdf = new SC\eHtml2Pdf($html, [
    \(aqheader\(aq   => \(aq<p>#section# \- page #Page# of #ToPage#</p>\(aq,
    \(aqmargins\(aq  => [\(aqtop\(aq => 10, \(aqfirst_top\(aq => null],
    \(aqtoc_page\(aq => 2,
    \(aqmetadata\(aq => [\(aqAuthor\(aq => \(aqAccounts\(aq],
]);
$pdf\->save(\(aq/tmp/report.pdf\(aq);
echo $pdf\->pageCount(), " pages\en";
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/php/<api>/html2pdf.so
The extension.
.TP
.I /etc/php/<version>/mods\-available/html2pdf.ini
Loads it; the package enables it for every SAPI with \fBphpenmod\fR and
restarts php\-fpm when it runs.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/doc/html2pdf\-php/html2pdf.stub.php
Stubs for IDEs: add the folder to PhpStorm's include path (Settings > PHP >
Include Path) or to Intelephense's intelephense.environment.includePaths, and
SC\eHtml2Pdf and its options autocomplete.
.SH NOTES
The package is built for the PHP each Ubuntu release ships (22.04: 8.1, 24.04:
8.3, 26.04: 8.5).
It can't be installed together with simply\-cpp\-phplib, whose sc extension
declares the same SC\eHtml2Pdf: code written for one runs with the other.
